Task: Fix reward flatness + reduce entropy for five-station MAPPO

== Diagnosis ==
  500-ep training: 97% steps have n_granted=1, mean_reward flat, no improvement.
  Root cause is NOT the resolver (heuristic grants 5/5 at origin stations).
  Root: +5.0 base bonus makes all granted actions look similar after PPO advantage
  normalization. Policy has 24-60 legal actions at each step but can't distinguish
  good from bad. Random exploration picks bad actions 75% of time (dwell+120,
  plan+4 entry) → cascading delays downstream.

== Fixes ==
  src/env/reward.py: base bonus 5.0→0.0 (sharpen gradient), delay_coef 0.02→0.05,
    held penalty -1.0→-3.0
  src/experiment/run_train.py: entropy_coef 0.01→0.001 (exploit more, explore less)
  Verified: dynamic bounds at intermediate stations give 24/45 legal actions
    (vs 0 without the fix), confirming P1-3 works correctly.

Rationale: PPO advantage normalization already subtracts mean, so +5.0 doesn't
  help learning — it only adds noise. Sharper delay penalty gives clearer gradient
  toward "earliest entry, min dwell". Lower entropy prevents policy from wasting
  exploration budget on obviously bad actions.
